\description{
Get the two teams (home and away teams) for a single
college football game, with team identifiers, home/away designation,
winner flag, and the \verb{$ref} URLs to every per-team sub-resource.
}
\details{
Wraps the ESPN core-v2 endpoint
\code{events/{game_id}/competitions/{game_id}/competitors}. The competition
id always equals the game id. By default returns one row per team (two
rows per game). Each row carries the \verb{$ref} URLs ESPN publishes for that
team's score, linescores, roster, statistics, leaders, and record
resources -- the dedicated \verb{espn_cfb_game_team_*()} wrappers fetch
and flatten those resources for you. \code{curated_rank} is the AP/Coaches-poll
style rank ESPN attaches to the team at game time.

The \code{format} argument controls the output shape:
\itemize{
\item \code{"long"} (default) -- one row per competitor (two rows per
game), with the \code{home_away} column, as shown in the \emph{Value} table.
\item \code{"wide"} -- \strong{one row per game}: every per-competitor column
is pivoted to a \verb{home_*} / \verb{away_*} column keyed off the
\code{home_away} value (e.g. \code{home_team_id}, \code{home_winner},
\code{home_curated_rank}, \code{away_team_id}, \code{away_winner}, ...).
\code{game_id} stays a single key column, so a \code{"wide"} result is
directly joinable onto any one-row-per-game table.
}

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to every team-id column -- \code{team_id} and \code{competitor_id}. For
\code{team_id} the siblings are \code{team_name}, \code{team_abbreviation},
\code{team_location}, \code{team_display_name}, \code{team_short_display_name},
\code{team_nickname}, \code{team_color}, \code{team_alternate_color}, \code{team_logo_href},
\code{team_logo_dark_href}; \code{competitor_id} gains the parallel
\code{competitor_name}, \code{competitor_abbreviation}, .... \code{team_detail}
composes with \code{format} -- in \code{"wide"} mode the \code{home_team_id} /
\code{away_team_id} columns get \code{home_team_name} / \code{away_team_name} / etc.
too. A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the
wrapper. Set \code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the
join.
}
